        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are delighted to present The Mews at 123 Drimnagh Road. This an exciting new property - a brand-new, A-rated two-bedroom home that combines contemporary design, exceptional energy efficiency and beautifully considered accommodation.\r\n\r\nPresented in pristine, turnkey condition, this impressive home offers the rare opportunity to be the very first to enjoy a property built around modern standards of comfort, style and efficiency. Arranged over two floors, the accommodation is bright, spacious and exceptionally well suited to contemporary living, with a generous open-plan living and dining area, a sleek modern kitchen, two well-proportioned bedrooms, two bathrooms and a convenient ground-floor WC.\r\n\r\nThe home's A-rated energy performance is a standout feature, reflecting the quality of its construction and modern specification. Underfloor heating and an air-to-water heating system provide efficient, comfortable heating throughout, while the contemporary interiors create a fresh and stylish environment that is ready to move straight into. There is no work required and no compromise necessary.\r\n\r\nAdding further appeal is the excellent flexibility offered by the large garage. Providing substantial additional storage at present, it also presents exciting potential to create further living accommodation or a third bedroom, subject to the necessary planning permission. A well-sized private rear garden and first-floor balcony further enhance the property, providing valuable outdoor space that is increasingly difficult to find.\r\n\r\nThe result is a home that feels particularly well balanced: brand new, A-rated, beautifully finished and flexible, with excellent indoor and outdoor space. It will appeal strongly to first-time buyers looking for a modern home, young families seeking adaptable accommodation, and investors looking for a high-quality, energy-efficient property in an established Dublin location.\r\n\r\nDrimnagh is an established and increasingly popular location, offering a community atmosphere while remaining exceptionally well connected to the city centre. The area has a distinctive local character, with the historic Drimnagh Castle, providing a unique landmark close to home.\r\n\r\nEveryday convenience is well catered for, with an excellent selection of shops, cafés and services along Drimnagh Road, Galtymore Road and Errigal Road. Crumlin Shopping Centre and Ashleaf Shopping Centre provide further choice, while Lidl in Walkinstown, Aldi on the Long Mile Road and SuperValu in Walkinstown are all within easy reach. There is also a varied selection of cafés, restaurants and local meeting places, including Farmhouse Café, The Black Forge Inn, Eleanora Bar & Lounge and Coffee House on Drimnagh Road.\r\n\r\nFor those who enjoy getting outdoors, there is an excellent choice of green spaces and recreational facilities nearby. Lansdowne Valley Park, Brickfield Park, Eamonn Ceannt Park and the Grand Canal all provide opportunities for walking, exercise and leisure, while Willie Pearse Park and Good Counsel GAA offer further sporting facilities. Drimnagh Boxing Club and Crumlin Swimming Pool are also close by.\r\n\r\nTransport is another major advantage. The Luas Red Line is easily accessible from both Drimnagh and Goldenbridge, providing convenient connections towards Heuston, Smithfield, Jervis, Connolly and The Point, as well as west towards Tallaght and Saggart. Dublin Bus routes 122, 123, 151 and 73 also serve the area, with the 122 operating directly along Drimnagh Road and providing a particularly convenient connection towards the city centre, O'Connell Street and College Green.\r\nMullery O’Gara are delighted to present The Mews at 123 Drimnagh Road. This an exciting new property - a brand-new, A-rated two-bedroom home that combines contemporary design, exceptional energy efficiency and beautifully considered accommodation.\r\n\r\nPresented in pristine, turnkey condition, this impressive home offers the rare opportunity to be the very first to enjoy a property built around modern standards of comfort, style and efficiency. Arranged over two floors, the accommodation is bright, spacious and exceptionally well suited to contemporary living, with a generous open-plan living and dining area, a sleek modern kitchen, two well-proportioned bedrooms, two bathrooms and a convenient ground-floor WC.\r\n\r\nThe home's A-rated energy performance is a standout feature, reflecting the quality of its construction and modern specification. Underfloor heating and an air-to-water heating system provide efficient, comfortable heating throughout, while the contemporary interiors create a fresh and stylish environment that is ready to move straight into. There is no work required and no compromise necessary.\r\n\r\nAdding further appeal is the excellent flexibility offered by the large garage. Providing substantial additional storage at present, it also presents exciting potential to create further living accommodation or a third bedroom, subject to the necessary planning permission. A well-sized private rear garden and first-floor balcony further enhance the property, providing valuable outdoor space that is increasingly difficult to find.\r\n\r\nThe result is a home that feels particularly well balanced: brand new, A-rated, beautifully finished and flexible, with excellent indoor and outdoor space. It will appeal strongly to first-time buyers looking for a modern home, young families seeking adaptable accommodation, and investors looking for a high-quality, energy-efficient property in an established Dublin location.\r\n\r\nDrimnagh is an established and increasingly popular location, offering a community atmosphere while remaining exceptionally well connected to the city centre. The area has a distinctive local character, with the historic Drimnagh Castle, providing a unique landmark close to home.\r\n\r\nEveryday convenience is well catered for, with an excellent selection of shops, cafés and services along Drimnagh Road, Galtymore Road and Errigal Road. Crumlin Shopping Centre and Ashleaf Shopping Centre provide further choice, while Lidl in Walkinstown, Aldi on the Long Mile Road and SuperValu in Walkinstown are all within easy reach. There is also a varied selection of cafés, restaurants and local meeting places, including Farmhouse Café, The Black Forge Inn, Eleanora Bar & Lounge and Coffee House on Drimnagh Road.\r\n\r\nFor those who enjoy getting outdoors, there is an excellent choice of green spaces and recreational facilities nearby. Lansdowne Valley Park, Brickfield Park, Eamonn Ceannt Park and the Grand Canal all provide opportunities for walking, exercise and leisure, while Willie Pearse Park and Good Counsel GAA offer further sporting facilities. Drimnagh Boxing Club and Crumlin Swimming Pool are also close by.\r\n\r\nTransport is another major advantage. The Luas Red Line is easily accessible from both Drimnagh and Goldenbridge, providing convenient connections towards Heuston, Smithfield, Jervis, Connolly and The Point, as well as west towards Tallaght and Saggart. Dublin Bus routes 122, 123, 151 and 73 also serve the area, with the 122 operating directly along Drimnagh Road and providing a particularly convenient connection towards the city centre, O'Connell Street and College Green."
